Lisu Bosa is a free and open Lisu font family. Lisu script, also known as
Old Lisu or Fraser, was created in 1915 by Burmese preacher Sara Ba Thaw and
modified in the 1930s by British missionary James Fraser. Invented in China
to represent the Lisu language, the script travelled with speakers of the
language as they emigrated to countries such as Myanmar, Thailand, and
India.

Lisu Bosa supports the complete range of Unicode characters for the script.
The name Bosa means "easily written."
